    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dbf5453e_c4341c16",
        "filename": "acme/autocert/autocert.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-11T19:55:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "but we don\u0027t own the port. the user needs to start a listener somehow anyway.\nI would be in favour of not providing a fallback at all. if users want to serve content on the port, they can always do things manually, sort of acknowledging the intention:\n\n  http.HandleFunc(\"/\", myHandleFunc)\n  http.Handle(\"/.well-known/\", manager)\n  http.ListenAndServe(\":80\", nil)\n\notherwise, if they don\u0027t serve anything, they can just do:\n \n  http.ListenAndServe(\":80\", manager)\n\nwdyt? I\u0027m just afraid http.DefaultServeMux will be a common fallback value. see Sanjay\u0027s comment: https://github.com/golang/go/issues/21890#issuecomment-356839890",
      "parentUuid": "35f60a9e_60dc7886",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 239,
        "endChar": 21
      },
