        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-11T22:02:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still disagree. I think it\u0027ll be incredibly common for people to do their own things on port 80, such as redirecting to https. I don\u0027t want to unilaterally serve a 404 here. I don\u0027t want them to ever know about the substring \".well-known\" anywhere in their programs.\n\nMaybe we go back to a method to return a Handler, like:\n\n   // HTTPHandler configures the Manager to request \u0026 respond to ACME \"http-01\" challenges.\n   // It returns an http.Handler that responds to the challenges.\n   // It must be be running on port 80. If it receives a request\n   // that is not an ACME challenge, it delegates the request to the optional\n   // fallback handler.\n   // If fallback is nil, the returned handler serves a 404 Not Found response.\n   // Because the fallback handler is run with unencrypted port 80 requests,\n   // the fallback should not serve TLS-only requests.\n   //\n   // If HTTPHandler is never called, the Manager will only issue TLS SNI\n   // challenges.\n   (func *Manager) HTTPHandler(fallback http.Handler) http.Handler { ... }",
      "parentUuid": "a70b12ce_b477a63c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 239,
        "endChar": 21
      },
